+## Visual communication contract
+
+The diagrams use one deterministic SVG generator because the visual model is a
+maintained projection of the architecture. A protocol identity or plane-route
+change must make the generator check fail until the affected visual is reviewed.
+Hand-edited output would hide that dependency and permit the two color variants
+to diverge.
+
+The visual system uses ink, ivory, lapis, turquoise, mineral blue, bronze,
+saffron, pomegranate, and slate. It abstracts the restrained geometry and
+print-safe hierarchy of the project's publication references. It does not copy
+personal content, logos, calligraphy, or identity marks. Color never carries a
+decision by itself. Labels, designators, line styles, arrow direction, card
+geometry, and prose state the same distinction.
+
+The selected diagrams have three reading levels. The purpose map separates the
+ownership of MUSIC, NCP, and transport or device stacks before it shows their
+explicit composition. An overview then shows a causal or operational path at
+normal README scale. A separate invariant ledger carries the dense coordinate
+and equation set. Combining all three levels in one figure was rejected because
+it obscured ownership and reduced formal text to microtype. Removing the
+equations was also rejected because it would make the visual easier to scan but
+less exact.
+
+The causal plate keeps one equation at each numbered stage and one expanded body
+decision panel. It sends the retained sample to the observer through a separate
+dashed path that terminates at the observer symbol. The plant-feedback edge is
+thicker and uses a different route. This layout prevents a read-only evidence
+tap from being mistaken for a current-cycle control edge. The companion ledger
+retains the expanded common predicate, closed mode predicate, exact source
+coordinate, timing constraints, and physical-effect boundary.
+
+The historical performance plots reuse the palette but omit card decoration so
+data remains dominant. Direct labels replace a remote legend. Marker shape, line
+style, hatching, and an evidence badge preserve series and claim meaning without
+depending on color.
+
+The layout is screen-first and print-aware. The purpose plate uses a compact
+900-unit canvas. The causal and invariant plates use 1,200 units so their
+five-stage path and equation panels retain readable columns at the intended
+README width. The causal plate uses vertical semantic layers instead of two
+dense side-by-side equation blocks. A 12-unit source-text floor protects
+secondary labels, while the PDF atlas retains the native vector for detailed
+inspection. This floor is a layout guard. It is not an accessibility
+certification or a promise that every mobile viewport can show every equation
+without zoom.
+
+Each header separates evidence identity from the title. Three text-labeled
+capsules state the unreleased candidate, wire, and compact-proto FNV-1a-64
+diagnostic. The diagnostic is not the complete normative digest. A single long
+metadata line was rejected because it competed with long titles and became
+microtype. The grid and card lattice remain deliberately faint so they establish
+visual continuity without masking equations or connector crossings.
+
+### Diagram reading grammar
+
+Read each plate in a fixed order: title and evidence state, numbered path,
+supporting panels, then the boundary band. The following cues are redundant by
+design. A reader does not need hue perception to recover the structure.
+
+| Cue | Exact meaning | Why this cue was selected |
+|---|---|---|
+| Numbered designator | Stable reading order or named state within one plate | It supports prose references and prevents layout position from becoming the only identifier |
+| Directed arrow | Declared flow, dependency, or transition in the arrowhead direction | An undirected connector could be mistaken for authority in both directions |
+| Solid or dashed stroke | Primary path or a locally named observation, loss-bearing, reset, or invalidating relation | Stroke shape remains visible in grayscale, while the nearby label gives the exact local meaning |
+| Accent rail and text label | Plane, role, gate, or state class | The repeated text keeps color from becoming an authorization or status bit |
+| Filled or glowing card | Visual focus or restrictive state named inside the card | Emphasis guides reading without claiming success, safety, or implementation |
+| Lower boundary band | Invariant, evidence state, and claims that the figure does not establish | The claim boundary remains attached when a figure is viewed without its surrounding section |
+
+| Method | Benefit | Selection decision and rationale |
