-| Mathematical consistency | State scopes, equality rules, monotonic order, checked successors, and finite symbolic envelopes are explicit. A digest never substitutes for exact retained bytes. | B03 must allocate every numeric ceiling and exact projection. Model, implementation, and cross-language boundary tests must agree before rebaseline. |
-| Failure and crash recovery | Restart grants no Active authority, retired identities do not revive, and ambiguity never becomes success. | The durable generation issuer, no-reuse state, and disposition recovery profiles are not implemented. The compatibility idempotency key is narrower than the selected target. Fault campaigns remain later work. |
-| Plant safety and effect claims | Crebain owns final software admission, restrictive modes remain plant-specific, and protocol receipts stop at software boundaries. | The current body path is incomplete. Consumer safety cases and physical qualification remain external. |
-| QoS and overload | Lifecycle control, simulation-step, action, perception, observation, and extension resources have separate finite policies. Source correlation, step responses, and extension parsing have explicit reservations. | Exact scheduler, aggregate byte budgets, non-wrapping metrics, transport mappings, and load evidence remain B03 and implementation work. |
-| SDK buffering | Per-request bounds compose with a checked aggregate byte reservation and one finite pending-request count. | The TypeScript WebSocket client currently bounds only count. Browser and installed-peer load qualification remain later work. |
-| Extension isolation | A prepared activation and raw binary chunks keep extension parsing and load outside stable action semantics. | B03 must select the exact activation-context identity, its one-way derivation, and the delivery profile. Galadriel schemas and installed qualification remain later work. |
-| Evolution and compatibility | Stable-core, release, corpus, extension, and publication identities remain distinct. | B02 must authorize the rebaseline before any normative or generated contract change. |
-| Wire and schema parity | Each selected wire object has one source, generated forms, canonical projection, and cross-language corpus. | Current prototype source is not normative parity. B03 and N01 must select and generate the exact forms. |
-| Ecosystem dependency direction | Consumers pin NCP packages and expose thin role adapters. NCP imports no consumer application code. | Consumer work starts only after provider dependencies are ready. No installed role is qualified. |
-| Operability and observability | Bounded gaps, drops, supersessions, deadlines, terminal reasons, and insecure mode are visible. | Exact metrics, labels, persistence, and operator procedures remain B03 and deployment work. |
-| Documentation and visual traceability | Each figure has one reading order, redundant color and text cues, direct-view accessibility text, and a complete prose description. Equations define every symbol. | Figures remain informative. Render review and local checks cannot accept an ADR, qualify performance, or replace independent review. |
-| Claims and release state | Local code and tests cannot imply safety, interoperability, publication, or release authorization. | B01 independent review and every declared external gate remain unsatisfied. |
+| Deterministic hand-composed SVG generator | Exact layout, live text, light and dark variants, direct GitHub rendering, and reviewable source bindings | Selected |
+| Mermaid | Fast editing and good simple flows | Layout, typography, equation placement, and claim-boundary hierarchy are not controlled precisely enough |
+| Raster artwork | Predictable pixels | Text and strokes degrade under zoom, dark-mode pairing drifts, and source claims are harder to audit |
+| TikZ only | Excellent LaTeX mathematics and print composition | It does not provide the same direct README SVG, browser accessibility, or dark variant |
+| Hand-edited SVG output | Maximum local freedom | Generated pairs can drift, contract identities can become stale, and review cannot reproduce the artifact exactly |
+
+The generator enforces direct `<title>` and `<desc>` ownership, a registered
+asset inventory, no scripts or external resources, deterministic output,
+minimum typography floors, and at least 4.5:1 text contrast. Every public SVG
+has a light and dark form. Review at 720 pixels checks the normal embed, while
+full-resolution review checks equations, clipping, connector crossings, and
+edge clearance. Grayscale review checks that line style and text still carry
+the meaning. The PDF includes a full-page vector atlas on landscape pages
+throughout. The selected wide orientation keeps printed labels, five-stage paths,
+and equation ledgers from becoming decorative detail. These checks establish
+presentation integrity only. They do not validate protocol behavior.
+
+## 50-lens maintainer review
+
+This table records a maintainer-side first-principles review. It maps the design
+to fifty distinct failure and quality perspectives. It does not satisfy the
+independent review required by B01.
+
+| No. | Lens | Selected target | Current gap or required evidence |
+|---:|---|---|---|
+| 01 | Role and type separation | Simulation, plant, commander, observer, extension, and local-library roles are disjoint. | B03 must allocate exact role and descriptor identities. The current contract still has compatibility shapes. |
+| 02 | Identity scope | Realm, session, generation, stream, operation, command, package, and contract identities have explicit scopes. | Durable issuers and several exact projections remain implementation work. |
+| 03 | Causal correlation | Every source-bound command and observation-plane frame binds the exact source coordinate. Open-loop commands and pull replies bind an explicitly permitted absence. Arrival order and latest-value fallback grant nothing. | The reference loop proves the source-bound case locally. Complete disposition-to-next-sample correlation remains proposed. |
+| 04 | Authentication | Production ingress derives actor context only from verified transport evidence. | Direct Zenoh remote-principal extraction is unavailable. Live mTLS evidence is **NOT RUN**. |
+| 05 | Authorization | Installed default-deny manifests and live receiver-minted capabilities gate each route and plane. | Current helpers still accept host-supplied evidence. A-direct is not implemented. |
+| 06 | Trust termination | A forwarding hop terminates and reissues trust or carries an explicitly verified signed envelope. | Custody and forwarding profiles remain B03 and implementation work. |
+| 07 | Version identity | Canonical same-major wire identity and exact stable-core identity are required together. | B02 must authorize any normative rebaseline. |
+| 08 | Raw parser order | Frame, depth, member, key, string, numeric, and aggregate limits apply before semantic allocation. | Every production parser still needs refinement and allocation-path evidence. |
+| 09 | Canonicalization | Exact canonical bytes and named digest domains prevent ambiguous signing or replay. | Complete source generation and cross-language canonical parity remain future work. |
+| 10 | Replay and idempotency | Stream positions, operation identities, request bytes, and retained results are compared exactly. | Compatibility lifecycle keys are narrower, and the result-digest projection remains open. |
+| 11 | Lifecycle | One namespace owner preserves lineage through pending, ambiguous, terminal, and retired states. | Durable generation issue, atomic commit, and complete handover are not implemented. |
+| 12 | Currentness and revocation | Session, security, manifest, activation, lease, and observer-grant state move one way and are rechecked before effect. | Live rotation and revocation campaigns are **NOT RUN**. |
+| 13 | Error precedence | Raw and generic admission errors precede identity-sensitive diagnostics. Conflict never becomes a new admission. | B03 must freeze the complete diagnostic order. |
+| 14 | Clock discipline | Live deadlines use one receiver-owned monotonic clock incarnation. Cross-peer time is correlation only. | Installed monotonic clock, restart, and rollover profiles remain unqualified. |
+| 15 | Deadline semantics | Equality at an exclusive deadline is expired. Arrival never creates or refreshes command freshness. | Body-issued freshness grants remain proposed. |
+| 16 | Closed-loop causality | A later state sample closes an exactly correlated command-to-later-sample causal cycle. One forward hop is not a loop. | The installed Engram, Crebain, and Prisoma cycle is **NOT RUN**. |
+| 17 | Control stability | NCP retains timing and causal evidence but never infers stability from delivery. | Each deployment needs a plant, controller, delay, jitter, saturation, and fallback analysis. |
+| 18 | Software effect | Dispositions distinguish receipt, admission, application, restrictive latch, and unknown outcome. | The complete journal and executor binding are not implemented. |
+| 19 | Physical effect | Protocol evidence stops at the software boundary. | Plant qualification, actuator evidence, and physical achievement remain external. |
+| 20 | Fail-safe semantics | Restrictive behavior comes from the installed plant profile. No universal zero-safe action is assumed. | Crebain must implement and qualify each concrete plant action. |
+| 21 | ESTOP asymmetry | A current authenticated ESTOP can use its restricted lane. It cannot bypass envelope, session, or actor admission. | Physical interlock and reset qualification remain external. |
+| 22 | QoS isolation | Control, perception, action, observation, simulation, and extension work have disjoint finite capacities. | B03 must select scheduler and aggregate-byte values. |
+| 23 | Backpressure | Each plane has one explicit overload result. Action preserves restrictive severity. | Cross-transport load and recovery evidence remains **NOT RUN**. |
+| 24 | Memory bounds | Counts compose with portable bytes and local allocator charges using checked arithmetic. | The accepted numeric profiles and installed allocator measurements remain open. |
+| 25 | Allocation and copying | Prepared paths decode once and transfer one owned representation. Retained transitions avoid full-object copies. | Compact production framing and full-path allocation traces remain absent. |
+| 26 | CPU complexity | Hot lookup and owner transitions have finite complexity independent of unrelated tenants. | B03 must cap collision sets and select concrete structures. |
+| 27 | Locks and concurrency | One short owner transition orders mutable state. No lock spans external work. | The reference runtime has not implemented the complete body owner. |
+| 28 | Queue fairness | Reserved cut and emergency cells outrank Active work. Perception has a finite service bound when restrictive work is idle. | B03 must select and test the fairness cap. |
+| 29 | Restart | Restart restores no authority, stream, deadline, or no-reuse state by default. | Durable issuer and retained tombstone stores remain unimplemented. |
+| 30 | Crash ambiguity | A lost reply or interrupted send retains the same operation and never becomes success. | Fault injection, kill-point replay, and durability campaigns remain **NOT RUN**. |
+| 31 | Recovery and reconciliation | Exact query results and bounded journals distinguish retained evidence from unavailable evidence. | Complete production recovery APIs and retention values remain open. |
+| 32 | Metrics | Gaps, drops, supersessions, expiries, conflicts, restrictive transitions, and insecure mode are visible with bounded counters. | Exact metric names, overflow behavior, and dashboards remain B03 or deployment work. |
+| 33 | Privacy and minimization | Observer and extension projections carry only grant-selected fields and source bindings. | Installed redaction and retention policies remain unqualified. |
+| 34 | Extension isolation | Raw package reassembly, semantic parsing, callback work, and stable action resources are separate. | B03 must select activation, schema, and callback profiles. |
+| 35 | Wire and schema parity | One source generates every accepted schema, binding, fixture, and manifest identity. | Proposed B01 examples are not normative production parity. |
+| 36 | Cross-language parity | Rust and TypeScript independently reject the same bounded semantic hostiles. | Two installed independent non-Rust peers remain **NOT RUN**. |
+| 37 | API ergonomics | Safe entry points require typed live-session and actor context. Diagnostic and raw paths are named separately. | Some current APIs still expose compatibility or host-provided context. |
+| 38 | SDK buffering | Pending request count and aggregate bytes are reserved together before retention. | The TypeScript WebSocket client now reserves 128 requests and 8 MiB of unsent UTF-8 payload; browser buffering and a selected deployment profile remain unqualified. |
+| 39 | Transport mapping | Each transport maps route, reliability, congestion, priority, and security without silent defaults. | Zenoh production-secure identity binding is unavailable. Other stable transports are excluded. |
+| 40 | Ecosystem dependency direction | Consumers pin NCP and provide thin role adapters. NCP imports no consumer application code. | Provider dependencies block every native consumer finalization task. |
+| 41 | Consumer migration | Runtime, descriptor, fixtures, transport, and receipts migrate together. Copied protocol files prove nothing. | Engram is in progress. Crebain, Prisoma, Galadriel, and Haldir remain wire-0.8 surfaces. |
+| 42 | Simulation provenance | Simulation output remains `calibrated_posterior=false` and `is_simulation_output=true`. | Scientific calibration and reproduction require separate evidence. |
+| 43 | Observer non-authority | Prisoma and other observers have no lease, action edge, or current-tick feedback path. | Native-1.0 observer qualification is **NOT RUN**. |
+| 44 | External advice | Model or assessor output can tighten policy only through authenticated, monotonic, reviewed transitions. | External models cannot certify any gate. Live integrations remain separate. |
+| 45 | Test and mutation quality | Boundary, hostile, transition, causality, and cross-language cases detect seeded regressions. | Fuzz, sanitizer, soak, duration, and independent campaigns remain **NOT RUN**. |
+| 46 | Performance evidence | Metrics name their clock, interval, sample set, quantiles, misses, toolchain, and machine. | Performance qualification remains **NOT RUN**. No zero-lag claim is permitted. |
+| 47 | Supply chain and provenance | Locked dependencies, package inventories, signatures, SBOM, and attestations bind exact artifacts. | Release signatures, SBOM, and provenance remain **NOT RUN**. |
+| 48 | Reproducibility | Generated outputs are deterministic and clean-room reproduction is separately verified. | Clean-room release reproduction remains **NOT RUN**. |
+| 49 | Accessibility and visual traceability | Figures have direct-view titles, descriptions, ordered flow, redundant cues, sufficient contrast, and prose explanations. | Render review cannot accept an ADR or qualify implementation behavior. |
+| 50 | Writing, release, and operations | Exact terms, equations, runbooks, handoff states, and claim boundaries stay synchronized. | B01 independent review, all external gates, publication, and post-publication checks remain unsatisfied. |
 
